# =============================================================================
# REPOSITORY WORKFLOW RULES (full version and rollback recipes: CONTRIBUTING.md)
#  1. Never develop on main. Every change goes on a branch:
#     phase/<n>-<slug>, feat/<slug>, fix/<slug>, docs/<slug>.
#     Major changes (schema, dependencies, refactors, deletions) ALWAYS get their own branch.
#  2. Merge only after `make check` passes, using `git merge --no-ff <branch>`.
#  3. Before every merge: run scripts/backup.sh (verified bundle outside the repo) and
#     tag main as backup/pre-merge-<branch>-<YYYYMMDD>.
#  4. Tag each finished phase (phase-<n>) and push branches and tags to GitHub.
#  5. Never force-push main, never rewrite pushed history, never delete tags or backups.
#  6. Roll back with `git revert` (or `git revert -m 1 <merge>`), never `reset --hard`.
#  7. Never commit secrets (.env), data dumps, or the reference PDFs; that's what this
#     file enforces below.
# =============================================================================

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reference reports are third-party copyrighted material: keep them local only.
*.pdf
reference/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
